  "question": {
    "text": "The number of the positive integral solutions <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> of the equation <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn></math> is <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></math>, then the number of all possible factors of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></math> is"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "8",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mn>24</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1.1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1.2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1.3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1.4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2.2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2.3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></math><br />Each of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1,2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1,3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1,4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2,3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br />can be permuted in <math><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo></math> ways<br />Each of <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1,1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>24</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2,2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> can be permuted in <math><mn>3</mn></math> ways<br />The desired number of ways is<br /><math><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>5</mn></math><br />Number of factors of <math><mn>30</mn></math><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math>"
